WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:06.958
Pharmaceutical quality teams work through controlled procedures, work
instructions, validation summaries and change records.

00:06.958 --> 00:16.870
Before a quality decision is approved, the reviewer needs the current source,
the applicable wording and a defensible record of what

00:16.870 --> 00:17.814
was checked.

00:17.814 --> 00:23.950
When that trail is fragmented, experienced people spend valuable time
reconstructing documentary context.

00:24.950 --> 00:32.582
A single quality process can depend on a standard operating procedure, linked
work instructions, validation material, approved change

00:32.582 --> 00:34.278
controls and historic revisions.

00:34.278 --> 00:35.974
A clause can move.

00:35.974 --> 00:38.094
A reference can be replaced.

00:38.094 --> 00:42.758
An effective date can change what applied at a particular time.

00:42.758 --> 00:46.574
The review problem is not simply finding a phrase.

00:46.574 --> 00:50.390
It is establishing the controlled relationship between the sources.

00:51.390 --> 00:58.250
Cortessa's target pharmaceutical-site deployment gives each authorised quality
specialist a dedicated, self-sufficient box.

00:58.250 --> 01:07.222
Local procedures, validation material, change records, ingestion, index,
on-device model and source viewer remain on that box.

01:07.222 --> 01:11.971
Audit and Ask run locally against the approved corpus.

01:11.971 --> 01:16.193
Author remains in development and requires further testing.

01:16.193 --> 01:21.470
Quality personnel control the working context and every approved revision.

01:22.470 --> 01:31.765
Specialist boxes are designed to connect through quality systems, validation
and change-control departmental nodes to an on-site hub,

01:31.765 --> 01:34.346
entirely inside the air-gapped site.

01:34.346 --> 01:40.543
This is the target architecture, not a deployed or validated
production-network claim.

01:40.543 --> 01:47.772
The offline contract and application foundations exist; authenticated
transport, key operations, scheduling, backup, recovery,

01:47.772 --> 01:50.870
assurance and rollout remain deployment work.

01:51.870 --> 01:55.247
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

01:55.247 --> 02:02.422
It works across the bounded quality corpus to surface a missing reference,
inconsistent terminology, uncertain effectivity, unexplained

02:02.422 --> 02:07.909
revision differences or a procedure that appears to rely on a superseded
source.

02:07.909 --> 02:10.863
Each candidate enters a controlled review queue.

02:10.863 --> 02:16.350
It is not automatically treated as a deviation or a finding of non-compliance.

02:17.350 --> 02:22.260
Each audit result leads back to the passage that created it.

02:22.260 --> 02:28.956
Quality specialists can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and
confirm revision and document state.

02:28.956 --> 02:34.759
If the evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:34.759 --> 02:42.793
Authorised quality personnel determine relevance, accept or reject the
candidate, and record the outcome through the existing process.

02:42.793 --> 02:48.150
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish GMP compliance or validation
status.

02:49.150 --> 02:57.535
Process context, product impact and the organisation's quality framework
cannot be delegated to a language model.

02:57.535 --> 03:01.728
Cortessa can expose the evidence route and uncertainty.

03:01.728 --> 03:06.969
Authorised quality personnel determine applicability, significance and the
required action.

03:06.969 --> 03:14.830
Cortessa does not release batches, replace the qualified person, validate
itself or provide MHRA approval.

03:15.830 --> 03:24.647
A quality-approved revision can carry signed identity, content hash, parent
lineage and approved audit context through its departmental

03:24.647 --> 03:28.076
node and, where authorised, the on-site hub.

03:28.076 --> 03:33.954
Conflicts remain explicit; the hub cannot approve or select a governing
procedure.

03:33.954 --> 03:38.853
Receipt does not validate, certify or automatically index a document.

03:38.853 --> 03:47.670
The receiving specialist governs import and use, while the local Ledger
supports inspection without replacing approved quality records.

03:48.670 --> 03:56.085
Measure time to the current approved source, citation completeness,
supersession visibility, accepted and rejected findings, correct

03:56.085 --> 03:57.939
refusals and reviewer effort.

03:57.939 --> 04:00.720
Record corpus preparation and setup burden.

04:00.720 --> 04:09.525
The result should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must be
remediated before any next stage.

04:09.525 --> 04:15.550
Evidence from the customer's own workflow is more valuable than a generic
claim.

04:16.550 --> 04:21.539
Bring one bounded, non-production quality workflow and the authorised
specialists.

04:21.539 --> 04:26.529
Test the evidence route and governed departmental exchange before expansion.

04:26.529 --> 04:32.017
Cortessa claims no pharmaceutical deployment, validated use or completed site
rollout.

04:32.017 --> 04:35.510
Start a conversation about a scoped evaluation.
